    "result_text": "The build passes with all tests green. \n\n## Summary\n\nThe create audit line now also logs `membershipLevel` and `membershipNumber`, keeping the previously logged fields (`id`, `customerCode`, `registrationDate`, `membershipLevel`).\n\nTo keep the code well structured and avoid duplication, I:\n\n1. **Extracted `MembershipNumber`** (`model/MembershipNumber.java`) \u2014 the membership-number formatting logic previously lived inline only in `OwnerMapper`. It now sits as a small single-responsibility domain utility alongside the existing `MembershipLevel`/`MembershipPoints`/`Tenure` classes.\n\n2. **Delegated the mapper** \u2014 `OwnerMapper.membershipNumber(owner)` now calls `MembershipNumber.of(owner)`, preserving identical behavior with no copied logic.\n\n3. **Enriched the audit line** \u2014 `AuditOwnerCreated` reuses `MembershipNumber.of(owner)` (mirroring how it already uses `MembershipLevel.of(owner)`) so the two derivations share one source of truth.\n\nThe `AcceptanceTest.coreAuditIncludesLevelAndNumber` test and the full suite pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
